---
alwaysApply: true
---

- Always prefer simple solutions.
- Avoid code duplication; before adding new functionality, check for existing similar code elsewhere in the codebase.
- Only make changes that are either explicitly requested or are clearly related and well understood.
- When fixing bugs or issues, do not introduce new patterns or technologies unless all current options are exhausted. If a new pattern/technology is added, remove any obsolete/duplicate logic afterward.
- Keep the codebase clean and organized at all times.
- Avoid writing scripts directly in files if the script will only be run once.
- Refactor files that exceed 200–300 lines of code; do not let files grow larger.
- Keep the code modular